ri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Insulin Signaling Cascade: Ligand Binding</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="364" name="Google Shape;364;p49"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="228600" y="1219200"/><a:ext cx="4495800" cy="5181600"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr anchorCtr="0" anchor="t" bIns="45700" lIns="45700" spcFirstLastPara="1" rIns="45700" wrap="square" tIns="45700"><a:noAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Insulin binding to the extracellular domains of the receptor activates the catalytic domain inside the cell.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="1100"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>The catalytic domain in one receptor phosphorylates Tyr residues in another receptor.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr indent="-342900" lvl="0" marL="342900" marR="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:lnSpc><a:spcPct val="100000"/></a:lnSpc><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="1100"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPts val="2400"/><a:buFont typeface="Calibri"/><a:buChar char="•"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr b="0" i="0" lang="en-US" sz="2400" u="none"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="dk1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Calibri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Receptor autophosphorylation allows binding and phosphorylation of protein IRS-1.  </a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="365" name="Google Shape;365;p49"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="457200" y="762000"/><a:ext cx="8229600" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/><a:tailEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="This diagram shows the four stages, from a to d, of the activation of the insulin-receptor tyrosine kinase by autophosphorylation.&#xA;Diagram (a) shows a top view of a pinkish-brown folded structure, with insulin, represented by a red ball, clenched in the left center. Below this structure is the side view, which shows the insulin inside the top left of the pinkish-brown folded structure, with blue, rounded projections coming out on either side. The projections cross over a yellow bar, outlined with blue lines on either side (top and bottom). Diagram (b) shows a larger representation of what is described in diagram a. Here, it is clear that the yellow bar is the cytoplasm, and the blue lines represent the plasma membrane. The two rounded projections coming out of the yellow bar (cytoplasm) represent “Inactive (unphosphorylated) tyrosine kinase domain” (left) in diagram c, and “Active (triply phosphorylated tyrosine kinase domain” (right) in diagram d. The rounded projection to the right is attached to three Ps, each in a green circle, and it is surrounded by hairlike projections – the Ps represent phosphorylation. In diagram (c), a globular blue mass has a green ribbon-like structure intertwined. On the green ribbon, there are red, white, and blue bulbs, labeled, Tyr 1158 at the top, Tyr1162 below that, Tyr1163 below that, and Asp1132 toward the middle. The text below it reads, “Activation loop blocks substrate-binding site.” In diagram (d), the same globular blue mass with a green ribbon and red, white, and blue bulbs, is shown, with the same Tyr residues shown. However, this time, a target protein, indicated by a small red structure is shown to the middle left of the mass, right below Asp1132. Tyr 1163 is to the right of that, and to its right is Tyr 1158. To the lower left is Tyr 1162. The text below it reads, “Triply phosphorylated activation loop moves dramatically, making room for the target protein in the substrate-binding site.”" id="366" name="Google Shape;366;p49"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWithShape="1"><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:srcRect b="0" l="0" r="0" t="0"/><a:stretch/></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="4684712" y="914400"/><a:ext cx="4306887" cy="5857875"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>